Four cores are a sensible starting point, not a guarantee of a fourfold speedup. We must check whether the UEL/UMAT implementation is thread-safe, whether the selected Abaqus parallelization mode supports it, and whether sufficient memory and license resources are available.

We should also reconsider generating thousands of full-field ODB frames. The previous 23+ GB database suggests there may be considerable output overhead.

