4. My recommendation

We should now proceed in this order:

Fix the NaN problem → verify physical loading on a short pilot → qualify multi-core performance → run the complete five-hole benchmark with at least 24 hours requested, if supported.

I would not approve another full production simulation until the numerical problem has been demonstrated to be fixed. The corrected job should produce real crack propagation, not simply complete 7,000 increments.

This is particularly important with our December 13 research freeze approaching. We need to spend HPC hours on physically meaningful results rather than repeatedly generating large, invalid databases.
